    "raw": "Phase change: 876 K, sublimation point of As(α) to As₄(g); ΔH° = 33.235 kcal/mol of As₄(g). \nHeat capacity (cal/mol·K) and enthalpy (kcal/mol) equations: \n298.15-3000 K: $Cp^{0} = 43.585 + 0.056 \\times 10^{-3} T - 3.878 \\times 10^{5} T^{-2}$ $H^{0} - H_{298}^{0} = 43.585 \\times 10^{-3} T + 0.028 \\times 10^{-6} T^{2} + 3.878 \\times 10^{2} T^{-1} - 14.298$ \nReaction equations (kcal/mol): \n298.15-876 K: $\\Delta \\mathrm{Hr}^{\\circ} = -63.572 + 4.135 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} - 2.896 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 201.600 \\mathrm{T}^{-1}$ $\\Delta \\mathrm{Gr}^{\\circ} = -63.572 - 4.135 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} \\ln \\mathrm{T} + 2.896 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 100.800 \\mathrm{T}^{-1} + 63.660 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T}$ 876-1600 K: $\\Delta \\mathrm{Hr}^{\\circ} = -100.884 + 6.927 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} - 0.584 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 75.600 \\mathrm{T}^{-1}$ $\\Delta \\mathrm{Gr}^{\\circ} = -100.884 - 6.927 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} \\ln \\mathrm{T} + 0.584 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 37.800 \\mathrm{T}^{-1} + 127.278 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T}$ \nSource: Data from Mah (73). ",
